  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <h1>Milestones</h1>
    <p class="kicker">What opened, what was published, and when.</p>

    <p>
      This page lists the milestones of the Library site, newest first. News
      about school trust lands themselves is in the
      <a href="/newsroom/">Newsroom</a>. The full week-by-week build log —
      every update, in its original wording — is preserved in the
      <a href="/librarians/changelog/">site changelog</a> in the
      Librarians&rsquo; Room.
    </p>

    <hr class="archival-divider" />

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Thursday August 13, 2026 — Reader pages reorganized.</strong>
        The Library reorganized its reader pages to lead with the subject —
        the land, the money, the law, the cases, the states. The Library's
        description of itself and its methods moved to the
        <a href="/librarians/">Librarians&rsquo; Room</a>. No factual content
        changed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>August 12&ndash;13, 2026 — A full audit of the Library.</strong>
        229 errors found across 441 pages; the findings are reported in full
        in <a href="/about/corrections/log/">corrections log entry 013</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Wednesday August 12, 2026 — The preview notices came off.</strong>
        The booklet was reissued as a second edition the same day.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monday August 10, 2026 — The booklet published.</strong>
        <a href="/booklet/">The Library in brief</a> — a 20-page portrait of
        America's School Trust Library — published August 10, 2026.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monday August 10, 2026 — The July 24 ruling published.</strong>
        The letter opinion of July 24, 2026, which granted the State summary
        judgment in Coos County 24CV38372, is published in full; see
        <a href="/court/oregon-current-case/">Oregon's current case</a> and
        <a href="/about/corrections/log/">corrections log entry 009</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monday August 10, 2026 — Site consolidation.</strong>
        The Library's two sites became one, at
        <a href="https://schooltrusts.org">schooltrusts.org</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sunday August 9, 2026 — Two ledgers, merged and renumbered.</strong>
        The Library's two public corrections ledgers were merged on
        August 9, 2026 and the entries were renumbered —
        <a href="/about/corrections/log/">corrections log entry 008</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monday August 3, 2026 — The founding board seated.</strong>
        On August 3, 2026 the founding board was seated and adopted the
        Library's governing instruments by unanimous written consent; the
        full dated record of every filing and board action is the
        <a href="/organizing/">organizational record</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tuesday July 21, 2026 — Incorporated.</strong>
        Oregon accepted the Articles of Incorporation on July 21, 2026,
        creating an Oregon nonprofit public benefit corporation
        (Registry No. 259005891).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sunday May 3, 2026 — The Library named.</strong>
        The site was renamed from "Schools of the Republic" to "America's
        School Trust Library." (The book stays titled <em>Schools of the
        Republic</em>.)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Early May 2026 — The site opened.</strong>
        The public library site at
        <a href="https://schooltrusts.org">schooltrusts.org</a> opened in
        early May 2026, with three rooms live: Reading Room, Atlas, Counting
        House.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Late February 2026 — The research began.</strong>
        The research behind this library — the booklet, the Sacred Compact
        white paper, the Vision essay, the per-state research — began in
        late February 2026.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="archival-divider" />

    <p>
      The complete week-by-week history, in its original wording, is the
      <a href="/librarians/changelog/">site changelog</a>. The Library's
      charitable registration, incorporation, and board formation are recorded
      on the <a href="/organizing/">Organizational record</a> and in
      <a href="/about/becoming/">Building This Library</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
